def merge_sorted_unique(a, b):
    result = []
    i, j = 0, 0

    while i < len(a) and j < len(b):
        if a[i] < b[j]:
            if a[i] not in result:
                result.append(a[i])
            i += 1
        elif a[i] > b[j]:
            if b[j] not in result:
                result.append(b[j])
            j += 1
        else:
            if a[i] not in result:
                result.append(a[i])
            i += 1
            j += 1

    # Append remaining elements from both lists
    result.extend(a[i:])
    result.extend(b[j:])

    return result
```

This function iterates through both input lists simultaneously, comparing elements and adding them to the result list only if they are unique. It handles cases where elements are equal by ensuring that duplicates are not added multiple times. After processing all elements, it appends any remaining elements from either list to the result. This ensures that the output is an ascending-sorted list with no duplicates.
